// Service keys for the app. Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (which is
// gitignored — NEVER commit it) and fill in real values. Keep placeholders
// NON-EMPTY: CI copies this example verbatim to build, and an accessor like
// `Secrets.required("KEY")` fatalErrors at launch on a blank value. For a
// service the app genuinely doesn't use, delete its line rather than blanking it.
//
// See the "Secrets & Service Keys" section of CLAUDE.md for how to wire these
// into the app (project.yml base config -> Info.plist -> runtime accessor) and
// for the separate list of CI secrets that go in GitHub Actions, not here.
//
// xcconfig treats `//` as the start of a comment, so a bare URL value
// (https://host) would silently truncate to `https:`. Escape the separator
// with the empty-substitution trick — `$()` expands to nothing at build time:
//   https:/$()/host   resolves to   https://host

// RevenueCat (subscriptions / IAP). RevenueCat dashboard -> API Keys -> the
// public "App Store" key for this app. Starts with `appl_`.
REVENUECAT_API_KEY = appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

// Aptabase (privacy-first analytics). Aptabase dashboard -> App Settings ->
// App Key. Format like `A-EU-0000000000` / `A-US-...` / `A-DEV-...`.
APTABASE_APP_KEY = A-DEV-0000000000

// Sentry (crash reporting). Sentry -> Project Settings -> Client Keys (DSN).
// Note the `/$()/` escape described at the top of this file: a DSN is a URL, and
// an unescaped `//` would truncate the value to `https:` — non-empty, so the
// accessor would NOT fatalError, and the app would silently report crashes
// nowhere. That is a worse failure than a missing key.
//
// This key was absent from this file while the profile's own code required it,
// and the cost was not obvious. CI copies this example verbatim to build, so
// every test run in the affected project crashed at launch with
//
//     Fatal error: Missing SENTRY_DSN
//
// before a single test executed — and the old exit-65 handler read that as
// "all tests passed". Months of green CI over a suite that never ran. Adding a
// key here is cheap; the profile also ships Sentry dSYM upload in release.yml,
// so a project on this profile is assumed to have Sentry already.
SENTRY_DSN = https:/$()/0000000000000000000000000000000@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
